WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.190
A nice bath during the day is the best.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.850
Now then.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.670
Thank you.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.570
Getting to eat my favorite kanpyou roll 
in the bath is also a marvelous thing.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.360
Yes, indeed.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.680
It would be splendid if these 
peaceful days could go on forever.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.120
Yes, hello?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.790
<i>Work! Stupid Kaoru!</i>

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.900
<b>Katana Maidens</b>

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:28.620
<b>Episode 15  Slothful Person's Honor</b>

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.250
I've completed the aradama subduing 
mission, you damn brute.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.770
I mean, president.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.080
Just who are you calling a damn brute?

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.330
Here you call me director.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.630
Good work. Now, about your next mission.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.950
Wait, wait, wait!

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.580
I've been running around like crazy without 
a break for the past four months!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.010
Give me a break already!

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.260
Now, about your next mission.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.640
Damn it! I've never seen you so 
obviously pretend not to hear me!

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.730
I'm having you lead the team as 
captain and you'll go to Gunma.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.310
Wait, I don't have a passport.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.530
Don't make fun of Gunma.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.830
Supposedly there is a 
secret hot springs there.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.820
Rejoice. I'll give you that break you've been
wanting after you complete the mission.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.290
Isn't that what you said?!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.230
<i>I said after your mission was finished!</i>

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:14.330
What does it matter? We can't 
find the aradama anyway.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.060
The signals my finder was 
detecting were too small

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.960
and we couldn't determine the exact location.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.880
Even Nene couldn't track it down.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.550
And the eyewitness reports were vague.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:30.370
In the end I tried the human-wave tactic 
of looking for it with my own eyes.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.980
As the subjugation leader I 
believe in the search team

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.670
and have prepared the optimum conditions 
and am waiting for the news

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.390
that the aradama has been spotted.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.310
<i>You use your legs and search, too.</i>

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.480
Right where it hurts.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.590
As things are, as long as there is 
even the slightest threat of aradama,

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:51.320
we can't indulge in civilian 
actions. Understood?

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.310
And that is why

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.300
<i>I've arranged a back-up</i>

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.520
<i>to give you a kick in your lazy butt.</i>

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.830
<i>Get ready for a surprise.</i>

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:06.320
God, everyone is so afraid 
of a bunch of lame aradama.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:10.900
Which means, Vice Captain Kiryuu,

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.840
before I use the ryokan as my lodgings,

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.390
I think I will make it look like 
I was searching for aradama.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.520
You could at least try to mask your 
true intentions a bit more, Captain.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.360
Now then, roll-call.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.330
One!

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.070
Two!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:26.800
Three!

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:27.550
Four!

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:28.360
Five!

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.830
All right, we're all here.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.280
We gained one?!

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.990
What are you doing here, Sayaka?

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:38.080
I finished my mission with Kanami early.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.870
So the director told me to come here.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.950
Itomi Sayaka, now entering 
under Mashiko Kaoru's command.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.880
What are your orders?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.880
Gosh, it was about five meters tall.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.130
It killed at least ten bears single-handedly

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:57.860
and had bright red blood drippings 
from its claws and fangs.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.410
That old man flourishes his 
eyewitness account more each time.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.110
We haven't even seen a single dead bear.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.940
The elderly do enjoy
talking to younger people.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.450
Is that enough?

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.350
I have finished gathering 
information from the eyewitness.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.450
I would like to proceed with searching 
now. What are your orders?

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:19.330
Right, well, go ahead and search for it.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.510
Roger.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.930
Since we cannot detect any regularity 
in the witnessed location,

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.750
I will extend the search range.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:31.340
But if we expand the area too much, 
will that not make the holes bigger?

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.140
I will double the scope.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:43.270
That is her physical ability even 
without using the Hachiman power?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.680
We can definitely expand two times with that.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.060
That overly serious weirdo.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:52.070
Do you dislike team member Itomi?

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.040
I'm not good with overly serious types.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:58.740
Though the reaction I get

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.640
when I tease the same serious type 
Hiyoyon the no-chest is super pleasant.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.830
I haven't seen her in so long.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:10.460
Anyway, I think you should apologize 
profusely to this Hiyoyon person.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:51.130
<b>Keep Out</b>

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.130
Okay, that's enough for today.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.220
The mountain gets dangerous 
when it gets dark,

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:58.050
so be grateful to your captain for ending 
things early and get some rest at the inn.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.530
You really helped us out, Itomi-san.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:03.310
Our search range dramatically expanded.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.710
But we didn't find it.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.300
We'll find it tomorrow.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.340
We're expecting good things.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.260
Unlike with the captain.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:17.070
Is it just me, or have my stocks hit 
an all-time low since Sayaka got here?

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.470
It is just you.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.600
Your stock was already at an 
all-time low before she got here.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:31.710
I will definitely find the aradama tomorrow.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.540
You can relax a bit, you know.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:42.680
No direct damage by this aradama has 
been reported at all in this instance.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.520
Sana's gaze can't reach 
you here, so take it easy.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.490
Missions are to be finished quickly.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.480
A Toji's duty is to destroy aradama.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.130
That's true.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.240
You're correct as a Toji.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.740
I don't understand what you mean.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.870
Don't worry about it, you don't need to.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.420
My skin just gets so shiny 
after being in a hot spring.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.880
Hey, what happened to Sayaka?

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:22.110
She did not return to the room after dinner.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.610
I wanted to ask her about her love interests.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:25.760
Right?

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.350
Okay, that's fine then.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:33.150
Jeez, what is she off doing by herself?

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.280
I-It's not like I'm worried about her

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.950
acting cold like she's venting 
her anger or anything.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.050
Speaking of, Nene's gone, too.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:08:59.490
That's not right.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.560
Do it like this.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.400
What are they doing?

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.990
You okay? You have to be careful.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.700
<i>So even she can look like that?</i>

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.420
Kaoru-chan? This is out of the blue.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.010
<i>You've teamed up with Sayaka a lot, right?</i>

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.620
<i>How do you usually spend your time with her?</i>

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.510
Talking about swordfighting of course!

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.230
Oh yeah, she even let me

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.760
<i>spar with her recently.</i>

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.760
<b>Kanami</b>

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.090
While Sayaka is intense, 
Kanami is even worse.

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.260
What a pain.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:52.270
I think I am actually worried.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.060
Because Saaya is with Kaoru?

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:58.610
Kaoru-chan tends to find 
things quite bothersome.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.500
There's no need to worry.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.740
Despite how she seems, Kaoru is a kind girl.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:07.350
After all, she's a member 
of the Mashiko family

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.700
that's been living with 
aradama for 400 years.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.750
Hey there, Sayaka, you afraid?

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.470
Fight, Itomi-san!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.850
Take the captain down!

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.500
What do you mean?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.060
Nothing really, when you go to a 
hot springs you play ping-pong.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.230
We're in the middle of a mission.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.620
Still so serious?

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:31.640
Dummy, resting and playing 
are part of the mission, too.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:32.930
Mission...?

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:39.730
Like this?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.090
Even with Nene by your side
you're still an amateur at playing.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:49.200
I'll show you how to really play.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.700
I'm pretty sure a flag
just went up effortlessly.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.330
Let's do this, Sayaka!

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.930
You're incredible, Itomi-san!

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:18.810
You are surprisingly weak, Captain.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.530
You only need a burst of power

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:27.410
to take down an enemy in one 
strike with Yakumaru Jigen style.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.070
Hey, wait a minute.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:38.210
With my okatana a brat 
like you can't take me.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.180
Resorting to refreshingly unfair tactics?

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.230
I respect you in the opposite sense, Captain!

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:43.460
Good luck, Itomi-san!

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.510
A junior dominating a senior!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:46.340
Please do not destroy the room.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:51.350
You have some nerve, prepare yourself.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.100
You will report this to the director.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.980
I beg for mercy.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:03.480
Like this?

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.340
Satsuki Yomi.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.800
President Souraku.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:38.310
<b>Tsubakuro Family</b>

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.630
I'm sure Tsubakuro-san was happy.

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.910
She likely had some regrets,

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:44.370
but even so, she was able to stand on stage.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:47.610
She was able to fight and die as a Toji.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.610
You understand Yume well.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.700
What are you going to do?

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:56.870
Now that Yukari is gone.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:01.460
Even if Yukari-sama isn't here, 
my loyalty will not change.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.460
How is the princess?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.170
She has wandered off somewhere again.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.720
<b>Keep Out</b>

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.560
Now then, we will investigate the B route.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.850
We will contact you immediately 
if we find anything.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.430
Well, don't strain yourselves too much.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.480
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.490
Shall we get going then?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.050
That tickles.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:28.900
She's totally bonded with my pet.

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:29.690
Oh, that's right.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.610
Nene has gotten attached to Sayaka.

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:38.950
Which means that Sayaka has more of 
a future than Hiyoyon's flat-chest.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.010
And, sent.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.960
<b>That's it.
 I'm going to kill you.</b>

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.250
This is definitely the best.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.300
Are you okay?

00:13:56.300 --> 00:14:00.180
I-I'm totally... fine.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.130
I can keep going.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.520
Sorry, I lied.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.820
You don't get to say 
anything being over there.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.990
You can understand what its saying?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.950
I can't, but I can understand 
what it's trying to say.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:39.530
Is this the aradama that's been 
causing all the fuss around here?

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:41.730
About time.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.150
I guess there's nothing for it when it was

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.020
such a small signal that 
gave even Nene trouble.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:48.150
Go on, go back in the forest already.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.150
Don't just go carelessly doing things.

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:56.500
Why?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.910
A Toji's job is to destroy aradama.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.650
Yes, that's right.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:04.160
It's right, but I don't like it.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.210
Look.

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.290
Even Nene isn't showing 
any hostility towards it.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.410
An aradama is an aradama.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:15.150
If we leave it be, it might 
harm someone someday.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:18.050
I see, you may be right.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:22.090
Once it becomes an aradama, 
we have to kill it.

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:24.850
Okay. What about Nene, then?

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.020
According to you're saying,

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:34.080
we'd have to kill this utterly 
neglected playful little guy.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.230
Can you kill it, Sayaka?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.290
No, I can't kill Nene.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:54.960
Nene.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.300
I was mistaken?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.530
You're not mistaken.

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:03.490
That's how a normal Toji thinks.

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:05.390
But you do have to stop killing things

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.770
without thinking about it 
just because you're a Toji.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.360
Really think things through before you kill.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:15.400
There might be other aradama like this one.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.280
Think before I kill?

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:22.650
At least, that's how the Mashiko clan 
has been doing things for years.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:27.950
But I only realized that I was 
doing this myself just recently

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:30.170
so I can't really talk down to you about it.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.950
I still don't really understand.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:38.800
But I do want to think things through.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.800
That's enough for now.

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:45.560
But what do we do about this aradama?

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:49.600
Basically you need to think of 
an aradama like a wild bear.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:53.940
As long as you stay away from its territory 
you won't need to track it down.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:56.320
Is that you've been abandoning the mission?

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:59.160
No, I just normally avoid working.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.070
Now then, what'll we say to the president?

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:07.990
Nene?

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:08.660
What's wrong?

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:17.750
Why did that suddenly happen?

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:22.110
Dunno, but that's not the 
aradama from before anymore.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:23.680
No...

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:26.880
The Mashiko history is 
pretty sketchy on this.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.930
That's why I also know 
where to draw the line.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.170
Kaoru!

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.940
Think, believe, and when that is not enough,

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:43.660
take on its bared fangs and 
face it with your sword.

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:46.270
That is the Mashiko's distinction.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.400
So I'll do it.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:05.950
The noro is supposed to be 
enshrined in a local shrine.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:11.890
We will handle the collection and 
guarding of it. You two please rest.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.680
Are we really okay to be heading back first?

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.990
There's a Toji who steals noro.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.990
Yeah, that's right.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:27.840
But they won't go after such lame 
noro so deep in the woods like this.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:32.950
Besides, you can really rely on 
motivated people to handle anything.

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:37.330
Well, now that the mission is 
over, shall we play for real?

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:42.630
Damn it, the hits just keep on coming!

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:01.780
We finally meet.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:04.610
The scent of this noro...

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:08.490
I see, so you were the one 
who has been following me?

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:15.420
Give back the noro you've stolen.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:28.930
Then...

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.810
Curse you,

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.560
that's the Niten Ichi style!

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.740
I can feel it coming from your okatana.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:42.920
Is it longing? Grief? Anger? No, hesitation?

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:47.030
It seems that you cannot 
even make up your own mind.

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:48.910
Be quiet!

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:01.840
I just have to last for a moment!

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.910
Is that also part of the 
cause of your hesitation?

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.640
I told you to be quiet!

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:23.310
You have rather piqued 
my interest, Shidou Maki.

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:24.290
Wait!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.370
Hey, are you guys still alive?!

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.290
They've just fainted.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.790
I knew it, you're—

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:39.360
Shidou Maki.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.170
Did you do this to them?

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:47.130
Hey, wait!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:50.180
Kaoru, the noro is gone.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.330
Damn it, curse her.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:03.600
They're okay. They just 
used up their utsushi.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:06.900
It was that hooded figure.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:10.280
Yeah, it was definitely Shidou Maki.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:13.630
I'm sorry though, we lost the noro.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:16.320
<i>I see, good work.</i>

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.870
That's it? You're not mad?

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:23.220
<i>You destroyed the aradama and took 
care of peoples' concerns, right?</i>

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.830
<i>Then there's no problem.</i>

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:29.070
I believed you! Director, I mean, old lady!

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:31.110
<i>Hey, that correction wasn't 
necessary now, was it?</i>

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:35.540
<i>Why are you calling me old lady? 
You'll be an old lady some day, too!</i>

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:35.540
Here, you report to her, too.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:36.470
<i>Are you listening to me?!</i>

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:37.530
Hello?

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:43.310
<i>A-Ah, sorry, Sayaka,
for making you deal with her.</i>

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.590
She taught me something 
valuable about being a Toji.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:50.320
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.130
She said playing was also 
part of the mission.

00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:56.070
<i>Okay, give me back to Kaoru.</i>

00:21:56.070 --> 00:21:57.700
Dash!

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:01.670
<i>Hey, don't you run away, Kaoru!</i>

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:04.130
<i>I know that's what you're doing!</i>

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:39.800
<b>Next Episode Audience with the Warden</b>
